cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Heatpump-Pinch: pinch analysis, heat pump integration and techno-economics for industrial process-heat electrification"
abstract: >-
  Python toolkit and Streamlit front end for the electrification of industrial
  process heat. It computes pinch
  targets with individual temperature shifts, composite and grand composite
  curves, sizes heat pumps from the GCC, screens working fluids with a CoolProp
  cycle model, evaluates heat-exchanger network retrofits and performs the
  techno-economic analysis. Validated against published case studies.
authors:
  - family-names: Caldas
    given-names: Tomás
version: 0.8.0
date-released: 2026-11-11
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/TheJohn01/Heatpump-Pinch"
keywords:
  - pinch analysis
  - heat pump
  - process integration
  - electrification
  - techno-economic analysis
